EPIC-260720-21aq1i_declarative-compiled-builds/STORY-260720-3plyvy_curator-go-build-driver/TASK-260720-2284br_commit-installations-atomically/progress.md:149:REWORK CYCLE 4 (R5) COMPLETE, ready for review. R5 closed at its source in .temp/TASK-260720-1zntv0/worktree (base origin/main 17804ce; nothing staged, committed or published). ROOT CAUSE accepted as written: all four declaration observations digested the path, then read and parsed it as a separate operation, and every supported writer rewrites its manifest in place with os.WriteFile - manifest.writeJSON for curator add|remove and global add|remove, scopes.AddHybridDecl/RemoveHybridDecl for hybrid add|rm, and hand edits of Skillfile.dev.json - so an A to B to A rewrite around the read left both samples at A while the closure came from the transient B. FIX: one read owns the bytes and the generation. New internal/install/generation.go readDocument opens once, reads from that handle, and returns the payload with the generation OF THOSE BYTES; the parser is handed the returned payload, so the generation revalidated and the bytes the closure was built from are the same object. Byte-level entry points added to the owning packages so no loader reads a path twice: manifest.ParseBytes, devsub.ParseBytes, scopes.ParseHybridDecls, each the function its own Load now delegates to; Load keeps its exact contract for the read-only CLI callers. Call sites install.go:180,220,257 and global.go:81. The reviewer alternative before/read/after path-sampling protocol was rejected on inspection and the reasoning is recorded: before=A, after=A, parsed=B is the ABA case, so no number of path samples closes it. No control flow changed - recheck already routed any generation difference to restartClosure and runCommit already calls it under the home lock after journal recovery and before both cache publication and target staging. STRUCTURAL, not conventional: observations is now one record per key (generation + path + reader) instead of parallel maps, observation.current() is the single recheck door and re-reads through the reader that recorded the entry, and the four declaration keys have their own documentKey type - a document can only enter through observeDocument, which takes a generation, and cannot be passed to observe, which takes a path, so reintroducing the ABA-prone form is a compile error. TESTS: 10 new permanent cases. internal/install/generation_test.go locks the binding at the read for both writer shapes (in-place rewrite mid-read, and rename mid-read where the payload stays on the old inode and the recheck must see the replacement), plus content-addressing, absent, unreadable stability, and a direct recheck case. internal/install/aba_test.go drives the full A to B to A sequence through each documents real writer for project manifest, global manifest, hand-edited substitutions and hybrid activation: each asserts the restoration was byte-identical, requires the restart to name its observation, and proves no transient context, shim, adapter mirror, marker substituted field or consumer state committed and no journal survived. The transient generation is applied inside the single read through a one-shot afterDocumentOpen seam, nil in production, same convention as godriver.controlSeamFault; the seam fails the test if the window never opened. A byte-identical-rewrite control proves the fix does not turn every concurrent save into a restart. NEGATIVE CONTROL both orderings: with digest-before-read restored all four install-level ABA cases FAIL and fail by committing the transient declaration (skill-b installed, SUBSTITUTED recorded, hybrid skill-h installed, no restart message) and the in-place binding case fails while the control still passes; with the digest taken after the read the rename binding case fails. GATES on the final tree 19:50-20:08, standalone processes with durable exits: gofmt 0, diff-check 0, build 0, vet 0, test-r5 0 (15s), test-revalidation 0 (30s, the 6 R4 cases), test-loaders 0, reviewer cycle-2 hybrid and cycle-3 project/global repro overlays 0 unmodified, test-install 0 (190s), test-atomicity 0 (406s), test-rest 0 (29s), five race gates 0 with zero data races, pinned golangci-lint v2.4.0 repo-wide 0 issues and re-confirmed 0 after cache clean. NOT CLAIMED: test-godriver exited 1 (51s) on one subtest hitting the sibling-owned 15.02s wall-clock probe deadline with no assertion failure under load average 12+; isolated rerun of the same tree exits 0 in 28s. The cycle-4 ABA overlay is NOT re-runnable and is not claimed: it pins a pre-R5 copy of install.go and its two hook points name a window this fix deletes; that scenario is now a permanent test whose negative control reproduces the reviewer failure exactly. REVIEWER ATTENTION: two deliberate behaviour changes fall out of digesting bytes instead of a path - a chmod no longer restarts a run, and a symlinked manifest is now revalidated by content, where DigestPath previously refused the link and pinned it to an unreadable marker that compared equal to itself forever, i.e. a symlinked manifest was not revalidated at all. Darwin/arm64 only; hardened containment STORY-260728-327soo remains separate and non-gating and is not claimed.
